From: Romain Tisserand <romain.tisserand@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Makefile: build as gnu17

GCC 15 defaults to C23, where "void (*)()" means "void (*)(void)".
pigpio stores every callback as such an unprototyped pointer
(callbk_t) and calls it with 1 to 3 arguments, which is now 17
errors ("too many arguments to function", incompatible pointer
types). Build with -std=gnu17, the dialect the code was written for.

Buildroot passes CFLAGS on the make command line, so the flag needs
"override" to be appended.

Upstream: not applicable, pigpio has had no commit since 2021.
---
diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ STRIPLIB     = $(STRIP) --strip-unneeded
 
 SOVERSION    = 1
 
-CFLAGS	+= -O3 -Wall -pthread
+override CFLAGS	+= -std=gnu17 -O3 -Wall -pthread
 
 LIB1     = libpigpio.so
 OBJ1     = pigpio.o command.o
